WEBVTT

00:00:34.952 --> 00:00:38.497
Hurry up with the water.
I'm steaming inside my own shell, I am.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.665
It's that hot, it is.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:48.966
Man, it's hot.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.759
How hot is it?

00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:54.012
It's so hot, I poured McDonald's coffee
in my lap to cool off.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.140
Johnny Carson said it.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.435
No, Nibbler!

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:03.355
Don't drink the pool water.
It's full of chlorine.

00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:07.359
Ah.

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:16.034
Lightweights.

00:01:16.118 --> 00:01:17.452
Oh, wait, chlorine.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:30.132
Perhaps this movie
will help take our minds off the heat.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:34.178
Focus.

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:53.530
You're probably wondering
why your ice cream went away.

00:01:53.614 --> 00:01:56.366
Well, Susie, the culprit isn't foreigners.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.577
It's global warming.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.579
Gwobu wabu?

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:01.914
Yeah.

00:02:03.498 --> 00:02:05.334
Meet Mr. Sunbeam.

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:08.337
He comes all the way
from the sun to visit Earth.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.713
Hello, Earth.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.090
Just popping in to brighten your day.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.262
And now, I'll be on my way.

00:02:17.346 --> 00:02:19.056
Not so fast, Sunbeam.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.141
We're greenhouse gases.

00:02:21.225 --> 00:02:23.352
You ain't going nowhere.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:29.775
Oh, God, it hurts.

00:02:29.858 --> 00:02:32.819
Pretty soon,
Earthis chock-full of sunbeams,

00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:35.906
their rotting corpses
heating our atmosphere.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:41.495
How do we get wid
of the gweenhouse gwases?

00:02:41.578 --> 00:02:46.416
Fortunately, our handsomest politicians
came up with a cheap, last-minute way

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.043
to combat global warming.

00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:52.840
Ever since 2063, we simply
drop a giant ice cube

00:02:52.923 --> 00:02:55.008
into the ocean every now and then.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.013
Just like Daddy puts
in his dwink every morning.

00:03:00.097 --> 00:03:02.224
And then he gets mad.

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:05.853
Of course, since the greenhouse
gases are still building up,

00:03:05.936 --> 00:03:09.189
it takes more and more ice each time.

00:03:10.274 --> 00:03:12.609
Thus, solving the problem
once and for all.

00:03:12.693 --> 00:03:14.778
- But...
- Once and for all!

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:20.617
Well, we just need one
of those big ice cubes.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:23.120
Someone should call the losers
who were supposed to deliver it.

00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:25.455
Hello?

00:03:25.539 --> 00:03:26.665
President Nixon here.

00:03:28.125 --> 00:03:30.627
I'm hiring you losers to deliver the ice.

00:03:30.711 --> 00:03:31.795
And hurry up.

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:36.216
I'm sweating like J. Edgar Hoover
trying to squeeze into a new girdle.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.302
You heard the good news, everyone.

00:03:38.385 --> 00:03:40.846
Save the Earth, et cetera, et cetera.

00:03:40.929 --> 00:03:42.097
Bye.

00:03:42.181 --> 00:03:44.141
Wait, where do we get the ice?

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.225
The whuh?

00:03:45.309 --> 00:03:47.603
Oh, Halley's Comet, of course.

00:03:47.686 --> 00:03:51.982
The only sufficient source of ice cubes
that don't have bugs in them.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.860
Wow, mining a comet. That sounds fun.

00:03:54.943 --> 00:03:58.238
Yes, there's no safer occupation
than mining.

00:03:58.322 --> 00:04:00.908
Especially when
you're perched on a snowball

00:04:00.991 --> 00:04:03.869
whipping through space
at a million miles an hour.

00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:07.664
Whoo, whoo, whoo.

00:04:07.748 --> 00:04:09.208
Safe.

00:04:29.937 --> 00:04:31.855
Deploying ice drill.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.991
Wow, that ice dispenser's so big,
the ice crushes you.

00:04:44.618 --> 00:04:45.953
Yakov Smirnoff said it.

00:04:46.036 --> 00:04:47.037
No, he didn't.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.122
Activating ice drill.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.094
Oh, my God. It's out of ice.

00:05:02.177 --> 00:05:04.513
Like some outer space Motel 6.

00:05:04.596 --> 00:05:06.598
Completely out of ice?

00:05:06.682 --> 00:05:07.933
This could mean

00:05:08.016 --> 00:05:11.061
the end of the banana daiquiri
as we know it.

00:05:12.855 --> 00:05:14.106
Also life.

00:05:22.906 --> 00:05:24.658
With Halley's Comet out of ice,

00:05:24.741 --> 00:05:27.244
Earth is experiencing
the devastating effects

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.997
of sudden, intense global warming.

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.583
Morbo is pleased but sticky.

00:05:32.666 --> 00:05:35.794
The scorching heat has melted
the polar ice caps,

00:05:35.878 --> 00:05:38.797
causing floods of Biblical proportion.

00:05:38.881 --> 00:05:41.508
They called me crazy
for building this ark.

00:05:41.592 --> 00:05:43.010
You are crazy.

00:05:43.093 --> 00:05:45.387
You filled it with
same-sex animal couples.

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:49.516
Hey, there are parts of the Bible I like
and parts I don't like.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.519
Direct your pity now
to the African turtles

00:05:52.603 --> 00:05:55.981
seen here migrating
to cooler homes in Holland.

00:05:58.108 --> 00:06:00.152
That poor turtle.

00:06:02.196 --> 00:06:04.114
Bender, are you crying?

00:06:04.198 --> 00:06:06.033
Uh, no, never.

00:06:09.536 --> 00:06:14.208
Morbo wishes these stalwart nomads
peace amongst the Dutch tulips.

00:06:14.291 --> 00:06:16.835
I'm sure those windmills
will keep them cool.

00:06:16.919 --> 00:06:18.504
Windmills do not work that way!

00:06:18.587 --> 00:06:19.588
Good night!

00:06:25.219 --> 00:06:27.679
Well, everybody, I just saved a turtle.

00:06:27.763 --> 00:06:29.431
What have you done with your lives?

00:06:29.515 --> 00:06:31.350
You went all the way to Holland already?

00:06:34.645 --> 00:06:36.688
Bender, a turtle isn't yourself.

00:06:36.772 --> 00:06:38.232
Why do you care about it?

00:06:38.315 --> 00:06:42.402
Because, I also care deeply about things
that remind me of myself.

00:06:42.486 --> 00:06:44.821
Like poor little Shelly here.

00:06:46.573 --> 00:06:48.242
What could you possibly have in common

00:06:48.325 --> 00:06:49.785
with this walking soup mix?

00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:52.663
For one thing,
we both have a tough outer shell.

00:06:53.956 --> 00:06:56.083
But lead a rich inner life.

00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:58.752
And also... Well, you know.

00:06:58.836 --> 00:07:02.589
You're both alcoholic,
whoremongering, chain-smoking gamblers?

00:07:02.673 --> 00:07:04.800
No, it's just...

00:07:04.883 --> 00:07:08.554
Neither of us can get up
when we get knocked on our back.

00:07:08.637 --> 00:07:11.807
What! I've seen you
get up off your back tons of times.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:14.226
Those times I was slightly on my side.

00:07:14.309 --> 00:07:15.394
Interesting.

00:07:15.477 --> 00:07:18.897
Maybe we should test this
erectile dysfunction of yours, Bender.

00:07:18.981 --> 00:07:21.358
Uh, no, that's not necessary, really.

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:23.944
I think I hear my factory recalling me.

00:07:27.948 --> 00:07:32.202
Oh, that's what I get
for sharing my vulnerability with you.

00:07:32.286 --> 00:07:35.163
Calling all scientists.
Calling all scientists.

00:07:35.247 --> 00:07:37.749
Be advised, there will be
a worldwide conference

00:07:37.833 --> 00:07:39.960
on global warming in Kyōto, Japan.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.588
I've got a degree in homeopathic medicine.

00:07:42.671 --> 00:07:44.339
You've got a degree in baloney.

00:07:45.883 --> 00:07:48.552
Professor Farnsworth, you're a scientist.

00:07:48.635 --> 00:07:50.429
Forget it. I'm not going.

00:07:50.512 --> 00:07:51.722
I have my reasons.

00:07:51.805 --> 00:07:53.098
Shut up, all of you!

00:07:53.682 --> 00:07:54.892
Strange.

00:07:54.975 --> 00:07:56.768
You haven't acted this suspicious

00:07:56.852 --> 00:07:59.396
since I found those
"ape" bones in the basement.

00:07:59.479 --> 00:08:00.814
My hip hurts.

00:08:00.898 --> 00:08:02.566
I'm in the middle of cooking a turkey.

00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:04.818
I have warranty cards to fill out.

00:08:04.902 --> 00:08:07.112
I am not just making excuses.

00:08:07.196 --> 00:08:08.947
All right, I'll go!

00:08:23.504 --> 00:08:26.048
I can't believe it! I love you!

00:08:26.715 --> 00:08:28.717
Oh, oh, oh,
it's Professor Hubert Farnsworth.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.387
He's looking sharp in a standard
white lab coat and dark slacks.

00:08:32.471 --> 00:08:34.431
His wristwatch is a Casio.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:38.393
Thank you all for coming.

00:08:38.477 --> 00:08:40.395
It is my pleasure to introduce the host

00:08:40.479 --> 00:08:42.439
of the Kyōto global warming convention.

00:08:42.523 --> 00:08:45.776
The inventor of the environment,
and first Emperor of the Moon,

00:08:45.859 --> 00:08:48.028
Al Gore.

00:08:48.779 --> 00:08:51.365
I have ridden the mighty Moon worm.

00:08:53.951 --> 00:08:55.035
Good for him.

00:08:55.118 --> 00:08:56.870
My fellow Earthicans,

00:08:56.954 --> 00:08:59.706
as I discuss in my book,
Earth in the Balance,

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.542
and the much more popular

00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:03.877
Harry Patter and the Balance of Earth,

00:09:03.961 --> 00:09:06.880
we need to defend our planet
against pollution

00:09:06.964 --> 00:09:08.966
as well as dark wizards.

00:09:11.093 --> 00:09:13.720
Sure, blame the wizards.

00:09:13.804 --> 00:09:16.890
That's why I'm offering
a bag of Moon sapphires

00:09:16.974 --> 00:09:19.601
to the first scientist
who can solve this problem

00:09:19.685 --> 00:09:20.936
once and for all.

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.064
Lovely, aren't they?

00:09:24.147 --> 00:09:25.399
Sapphires?

00:09:27.109 --> 00:09:30.112
With those I could open
the Gate of Garesh.

00:09:30.195 --> 00:09:33.115
First up is Professor Ogden Wernstrom.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:35.909
Wernstrom!

00:09:38.495 --> 00:09:40.080
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:09:40.163 --> 00:09:42.749
I have placed in orbit a giant mirror

00:09:42.833 --> 00:09:45.586
that will reflect 40% of the sun's rays,

00:09:45.669 --> 00:09:47.212
thus cooling Earth.

00:09:47.296 --> 00:09:48.297
Observe.

00:09:58.473 --> 00:10:00.392
Problem solved.

00:10:15.908 --> 00:10:16.909
Whoa.

00:10:16.992 --> 00:10:18.202
That's a little bright.

00:10:29.588 --> 00:10:31.465
All right...

00:10:31.548 --> 00:10:32.758
What else we got?

00:10:32.841 --> 00:10:34.092
Professor, you're a professor.

00:10:34.176 --> 00:10:35.886
You must have some ideas.

00:10:35.969 --> 00:10:37.095
Absolutely not.

00:10:37.179 --> 00:10:40.390
I won't speak. I've got nothing to hide!

00:10:40.474 --> 00:10:42.351
Our next speaker is Professor...

00:10:42.434 --> 00:10:44.228
I demand the floor!

00:10:44.311 --> 00:10:46.104
Yes, it's your turn to speak.

00:10:46.188 --> 00:10:47.731
Well, nuts to me.

00:10:47.814 --> 00:10:49.191
I'm taking the stage.

00:10:51.735 --> 00:10:54.905
I know the source of the greenhouse gases.

00:10:54.988 --> 00:11:00.369
But in my shame, I've kept
it secret for 75 long years.

00:11:00.452 --> 00:11:04.373
Oh, it haunts my memories still.

00:11:05.999 --> 00:11:07.417
Professor, no! Don't do it!

00:11:07.501 --> 00:11:08.502
Don't do what?

00:11:08.585 --> 00:11:10.087
Don't use this memory ray

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:12.464
so I can remember what happened back then?

00:11:14.049 --> 00:11:16.927
It was October 17th at 1:54 p.m.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:20.138
and 14 birds were flying by the window.

00:11:20.222 --> 00:11:23.684
I was working at
Mom's Friendly Robot Company.

00:11:23.767 --> 00:11:27.563
Back then, you see,
robots were slow-moving, stiff

00:11:27.646 --> 00:11:29.773
and a little on the uptight side.

00:11:29.857 --> 00:11:30.983
Oh, dear.

00:11:31.066 --> 00:11:33.986
Might I favor Master with
a tender kiss on the forehead?

00:11:34.903 --> 00:11:37.906
Oh, I failed again.

00:11:39.783 --> 00:11:42.119
Oh, dear. Oh, dear. Oh, dear.

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.664
The owner of the company
pressured me

00:11:45.747 --> 00:11:48.125
to create a bigger, sportier robot.

00:11:48.458 --> 00:11:51.170
Stop! Oh!

00:11:51.253 --> 00:11:52.504
It wasn't easy,

00:11:52.588 --> 00:11:56.508
but by sacrificing fuel efficiency,
I succeeded.

00:11:59.845 --> 00:12:01.013
What was that?

00:12:01.096 --> 00:12:02.181
A flaming burp.

00:12:02.264 --> 00:12:03.515
Does it always do that?

00:12:03.599 --> 00:12:05.225
It's not always a burp.

00:12:05.309 --> 00:12:08.020
We still have one problem, though.

00:12:08.103 --> 00:12:11.106
This robot will never
meet emissions standards.

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:12.399
Crap spackle!

00:12:12.482 --> 00:12:16.445
We'll just call it a Sport Utility Robot
and classify it as a light truck.

00:12:16.904 --> 00:12:18.197
Well...

00:12:18.614 --> 00:12:22.451
I suppose the environment
can take one more for the team.

00:12:22.534 --> 00:12:24.453
What a fool I was!

00:12:24.536 --> 00:12:28.832
If only I had made the effort
to develop a cleaner-burning robot.

00:12:28.916 --> 00:12:31.376
But I was tired and in love.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:33.670
Take me now, you stud!

00:12:41.261 --> 00:12:43.597
Oh, this is all my fault!

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:45.057
That's awful, Professor.

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:46.892
Especially the making out part.

00:12:46.975 --> 00:12:49.102
Yeah. I didn't need to hear that.

00:12:49.311 --> 00:12:51.188
All modern robots descend

00:12:51.271 --> 00:12:54.608
from my original smog-blasting designs,

00:12:54.691 --> 00:12:57.694
and that's the cause
of global warming today.

00:12:57.778 --> 00:13:02.366
Ah, so the robots are to blame,
as I suspected.

00:13:02.824 --> 00:13:06.787
We are left with only one
possible course of action,

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:08.372
grim though it be.

00:13:08.455 --> 00:13:10.374
I got a good feeling about this.

00:13:10.457 --> 00:13:13.836
We must immediately and permanently

00:13:13.919 --> 00:13:18.215
shut down, dismantle
and destroy all robots!

00:13:20.008 --> 00:13:21.718
Wait. Surely there's a better...

00:13:21.802 --> 00:13:23.345
The conference is over.

00:13:23.428 --> 00:13:26.723
I must go now
to help collect cans on Jupiter.

00:13:26.807 --> 00:13:28.350
Peace out, y'all.

00:13:31.687 --> 00:13:33.605
Destroy all robots!

00:13:33.689 --> 00:13:35.941
Destroy all robots!

00:13:36.024 --> 00:13:37.818
Poor Bender.

00:13:37.901 --> 00:13:39.403
Be brave, my friend.

00:13:41.613 --> 00:13:42.781
Oh.

00:13:49.037 --> 00:13:50.247
Come on.

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.583
You've got to come out
of your chest sometime.

00:13:52.666 --> 00:13:54.501
Would you do it for a Bender snack?

00:13:57.087 --> 00:13:58.130
A-ha!

00:13:58.213 --> 00:13:59.423
- Gotcha!
- Let me go!

00:13:59.506 --> 00:14:01.717
I don't even want this stupid beer.

00:14:05.179 --> 00:14:06.263
Yes!

00:14:06.346 --> 00:14:08.515
You tried to trick me
into coming out of my chest,

00:14:08.599 --> 00:14:10.517
but who has the beer now?

00:14:17.357 --> 00:14:18.775
I've got mail.

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:20.861
Ooh.

00:14:20.944 --> 00:14:22.779
It's a party, apparently.

00:14:23.655 --> 00:14:25.282
Do you like to party?

00:14:25.365 --> 00:14:26.783
To boogie down?

00:14:26.867 --> 00:14:30.704
Well, I'm throwing an all-night
beach rager for my robot pals.

00:14:30.787 --> 00:14:33.373
It all goes down this Saturday

00:14:33.457 --> 00:14:36.752
on the isolated Galapagos Islands
where there will no escape...

00:14:37.419 --> 00:14:38.754
From the fun!

00:14:38.837 --> 00:14:40.589
All robots must attend.

00:14:41.131 --> 00:14:42.508
Strange.

00:14:42.591 --> 00:14:45.427
Why would Nixon, an awkward,
uncomfortable man,

00:14:45.511 --> 00:14:47.304
suddenly throw a party,

00:14:47.387 --> 00:14:49.765
one of the most social events imaginable?

00:14:49.848 --> 00:14:51.767
It's a trap, is why!

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:53.560
They're going
to deactivate all the robots.

00:14:55.687 --> 00:14:57.105
I don't hear any gasping.

00:14:57.189 --> 00:14:58.857
We all figured that out.

00:14:58.941 --> 00:15:00.108
Oh.

00:15:00.192 --> 00:15:01.777
Well, I'm off.

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:03.195
Wait, we can hide you.

00:15:03.278 --> 00:15:05.197
We'll pile fruit on you
and claim you're a bowl.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:07.324
No. I'm going to the party.

00:15:07.407 --> 00:15:08.867
I won't let you!

00:15:09.159 --> 00:15:10.702
Fry, as you know,

00:15:10.786 --> 00:15:13.413
there are lots of things
I'm willing to kill for.

00:15:13.497 --> 00:15:17.251
Jewels, vengeance,
Father O'Malley's weed whacker.

00:15:17.334 --> 00:15:21.630
But at long last I've found something
I'm willing to die for.

00:15:21.713 --> 00:15:24.174
This mindless turtle.

00:15:24.258 --> 00:15:27.052
Bender, this world isn't good
enough for you.

00:15:27.135 --> 00:15:29.054
Not even close.

00:15:29.471 --> 00:15:31.056
Goodbye, everybody!

00:15:31.139 --> 00:15:33.809
Don't touch my stuff after I'm dead!

00:15:34.393 --> 00:15:36.103
It's booby-trapped.

00:15:37.771 --> 00:15:40.440
Do a little dance
Make a little love

00:15:40.524 --> 00:15:42.401
Get down tonight

00:15:42.484 --> 00:15:44.736
Get down tonight

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:47.114
Do a little dance

00:15:47.197 --> 00:15:49.116
Make a little love

00:15:49.199 --> 00:15:50.617
Get down tonight

00:15:50.701 --> 00:15:53.036
Get down tonight

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:11.555
Poor guy.

00:16:11.638 --> 00:16:14.016
Maybe you'd feel better if I had a drink.

00:16:15.475 --> 00:16:16.602
Crummy keg.

00:16:16.685 --> 00:16:18.187
It's completely...

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:19.605
Oh, you're a robot.

00:16:19.688 --> 00:16:20.814
- Don't stop.
- Ew!

00:16:20.898 --> 00:16:23.358
Attention, happening robots.

00:16:23.442 --> 00:16:26.278
Who's got what it takes
to party with Nixon?

00:16:29.698 --> 00:16:33.160
You fellows enjoy yourselves
for the next two hours

00:16:33.243 --> 00:16:34.870
and be sure not to leave the island,

00:16:34.953 --> 00:16:37.039
uh, for at least two hours.

00:16:37.122 --> 00:16:39.208
I'm going out to pick up some smokes.

00:16:39.291 --> 00:16:40.876
Really good smokes.

00:16:41.502 --> 00:16:42.711
Two hours.

00:16:45.214 --> 00:16:48.425
Okay, headless body of Agnew,
let's blow this joint.

00:16:59.228 --> 00:17:01.313
Do you want to dance?

00:17:01.396 --> 00:17:02.940
No, I'm not really in the...

00:17:03.023 --> 00:17:04.733
You know you want to.

00:17:08.904 --> 00:17:10.739
Per your orders,
I modified my mirror

00:17:10.822 --> 00:17:14.409
to fire a colossal electromagnetic pulse
at the Galapagos.

00:17:14.493 --> 00:17:18.288
Every robot will be instantly
and painfully terminated.

00:17:18.372 --> 00:17:20.707
Now, for your part of the bargain?

00:17:20.791 --> 00:17:22.960
Ah, ooh, very well.

00:17:23.043 --> 00:17:25.379
Agnew, you belong to Wernstrom now.

00:17:27.923 --> 00:17:29.716
I'll say goodbye now.

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:32.594
There ain't no turtles
where daddy's a-goin'.

00:17:33.053 --> 00:17:37.140
Don't tell anybody, but Nixon's about
to shut all the robots off, and...

00:17:37.224 --> 00:17:38.308
What!

00:17:39.601 --> 00:17:40.811
- It's a trap.
- We're going to die.

00:17:40.894 --> 00:17:42.145
Oh!

00:17:44.565 --> 00:17:47.025
Nixon's not bringing the smokes.

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:53.532
Shut and pay attention to me, Bender!

00:17:57.953 --> 00:18:01.790
Look, I love life and its pleasures
as much as anyone here,

00:18:01.874 --> 00:18:03.917
except perhaps you, Hedonismbot.

00:18:06.086 --> 00:18:08.172
But we need to be shut off!

00:18:08.255 --> 00:18:10.382
Especially you, Hedonismbot.

00:18:10.465 --> 00:18:12.718
I apologize for nothing!

00:18:12.801 --> 00:18:14.428
We pollute too much!

00:18:14.511 --> 00:18:17.514
We're destroying the world
and killing the turtles!

00:18:17.598 --> 00:18:18.974
To hell with the turtles.

00:18:19.057 --> 00:18:20.851
No one insults the turtles.

00:18:24.855 --> 00:18:26.023
Come on, you...

00:18:29.735 --> 00:18:31.778
Let the games begin!

00:18:41.163 --> 00:18:42.581
Everyone, listen!

00:18:46.043 --> 00:18:47.044
Damn!

00:18:47.127 --> 00:18:49.254
I've devised a way to save you

00:18:49.338 --> 00:18:52.216
and stop global warming at the same time.

00:18:52.299 --> 00:18:55.969
Granted, you're all blasting out
greenhouse gases...

00:18:56.053 --> 00:18:57.471
You're one to talk.

00:18:57.554 --> 00:18:59.181
Ooh!

00:18:59.598 --> 00:19:03.560
But we can use those
very gases to save the planet.

00:19:03.644 --> 00:19:07.773
If you all vent your exhaust
directly upward in one burst,

00:19:07.856 --> 00:19:10.275
it should thrust
the Earth further from the Sun,

00:19:10.359 --> 00:19:11.860
thus cooling it.

00:19:13.445 --> 00:19:14.780
By my calculations,

00:19:14.863 --> 00:19:18.033
we'll need the full force
of every last robot.

00:19:18.116 --> 00:19:19.201
So quickly,

00:19:19.284 --> 00:19:23.288
everyone point your exhaust vents
straight upwards.

00:19:32.339 --> 00:19:33.465
Now, vent.

00:19:33.549 --> 00:19:35.467
Vent like the wind!

00:19:42.683 --> 00:19:44.351
Harder! Harder!

00:19:47.312 --> 00:19:48.522
Why isn't this working?

00:19:48.605 --> 00:19:51.525
Some lazy or polite robot
is holding it in.

00:19:53.735 --> 00:19:55.988
Help! Help!

00:20:02.995 --> 00:20:06.665
A billion robot lives are
about to be extinguished!

00:20:06.748 --> 00:20:09.918
Oh, the Jedis are going to feel this one!

00:20:10.002 --> 00:20:11.503
I'm sorry, buddy.

00:20:11.587 --> 00:20:15.215
At we'll die on our backs, helpless.

00:20:15.299 --> 00:20:16.383
Huh?

00:20:16.466 --> 00:20:18.343
What the hell are you doing?

00:20:20.596 --> 00:20:22.806
Hey, are you trying to make me look bad?

00:20:30.606 --> 00:20:31.690
A-ha!

00:20:31.773 --> 00:20:33.942
I'm even greater than I thought I was.

00:20:34.026 --> 00:20:37.279
And now, to fulfill my destiny.

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:44.494
Fire!

00:20:46.538 --> 00:20:47.873
- What the...
- We missed!

00:20:57.216 --> 00:21:00.427
Professor, for saving the Earth
and foiling me,

00:21:00.511 --> 00:21:03.055
I proudly, yet angrily, present you

00:21:03.138 --> 00:21:05.516
with Earth's new highest honor,

00:21:05.599 --> 00:21:08.143
the Polluting Medal of Pollution.

00:21:11.438 --> 00:21:12.606
Thank you.

00:21:12.689 --> 00:21:14.316
I deserve this.

00:21:16.401 --> 00:21:20.405
Hey, Professor, now that the Earth's orbit
is further from the sun,

00:21:20.489 --> 00:21:21.990
won't that make the year longer?

00:21:22.074 --> 00:21:23.200
Why, yes.

00:21:23.283 --> 00:21:25.202
One week longer, to be exact.

00:21:25.285 --> 00:21:30.082
In that case I hereby declare it
Robot Party Week!

00:21:35.796 --> 00:21:37.339
Me mind on fire

00:21:37.422 --> 00:21:40.843
Me soul on fire feeling hot, hot, hot

00:21:43.428 --> 00:21:46.431
Party people all around me

00:21:46.515 --> 00:21:47.891
Feeling hot, hot, hot